{
  "version": 1,
  "units": "studs; Roblox axes (Y up); colours sRGB hex",
  "notes": [
    "Two-value lists are NumberRanges (min, max); size/transparency/color lists of any other length are sequences with evenly spaced keypoints over the particle life.",
    "Multiply Size, Speed, Acceleration, shape and light Range by the socket's vfx_scale.",
    "Texture names refer to art/vfx/textures/<name>.png; upload them and swap in rbxassetid://<id>.",
    "Beams: one Beam per entry of a kind's `beams`, from an Attachment at the socket (Attachment0) to one at socket position + `end` (Attachment1). Orient both Attachments with Axis = `axis` and SecondaryAxis = `normal` (the face of a beam with FaceCamera false). color/transparency are sequences from Attachment0 to Attachment1. Width0/Width1 and TextureLength scale with vfx_scale.",
    "Beam texture_speed is in studs/second along the beam (positive = start to end). Roblox does not document TextureSpeed's unit; if it is texture lengths per second, set TextureSpeed = texture_speed / texture_length (verify once in Studio).",
    "Beam textures put u (the image's width) along the beam and v across it.",
    "Emitters with shape_follows_width already have shape[0] set from the socket's width override.",
    "A kind's light is one PointLight in the socket's Attachment: Color, Brightness, Range (x vfx_scale), Shadows = light.shadows (default false); flicker/pulse are animated in game."
  ],
